<title>FRANCE: L'Oreal H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>L'Oreal H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>Profit before taxation, employee</p>
<p>	 profit-sharing and capital gains</p>
<p>	 or losses				3,086  vs	   2,753</p>
<p>    Operating				    3,435  vs	   2,991</p>
<p>    Financial expense			    302  vs	     229</p>
<p>    Turnover				    30,114  vs	  26,949</p>
<p>NOTE - L'Oreal said in a statement that its interim results for the first half of 1996 include Jade and Maybelline, two cosmetics companies acquired in the second half of 1995.</p>
<p>The rise in financial expense reflects the cost of the acquisitions, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
